1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,630
Ollie: Plip! The pebble sank right to the bottom.

2
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:11,120
Pip: But that big boat is not sinking at all!

3
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:18,400
Ollie: It's much bigger than the pebble, and it floats!

4
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:21,070
Ollie: Why do boats float?

5
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,520
Ollie: Let's find out!

6
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:03,750
Pip: I want to sail! Can I make a boat?

7
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:08,700
Ollie: Yes! A boat of your very own!

8
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:13,370
Ollie: It's tall and shiny! Let's go launch it!

9
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,960
Pip: Ollie, I don't think it's ready yet!

10
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:25,960
Ollie: Sorry, Pip. It's your boat. You tell us when.

11
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:32,850
Pip: Oh no. It's tilting...

12
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:46,190
Pip: My boat is no good. Maybe I should stop.

13
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:51,510
Gus: Don't stop! I've got a faster way!

14
00:01:51,910 --> 00:01:55,570
Pip: Gus, your faster ways always go wrong.

15
00:01:57,070 --> 00:02:02,920
Gus: Not this time! A boat needs to be strong. Strong like a lump of clay!

16
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,690
Ollie: A lump of clay?

17
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:11,460
Gus: Squeeze it hard, and it's a boat in two seconds!

18
00:02:13,410 --> 00:02:15,200
Pip: What if we try it the careful way?

19
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:21,770
Ollie: Let's watch Gus try first. Then we ask Gran Mari.

20
00:02:31,270 --> 00:02:34,770
Gus: Whoa. Where did my boat go?

21
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:48,920
Pip: Gus, your boat sank!

22
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:53,180
Gus: It didn't sink! It's a submarine! I meant to do that.

23
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:56,000
Ollie: Do submarines fall down and stay down?

24
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:01,230
Gus: Mine does. It's the best submarine ever.

25
00:03:02,730 --> 00:03:04,500
Ollie: But a boat should float on top.

26
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:08,000
Gus: It's not my fault. The water was too deep!

27
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:14,240
Pip: And my boat flipped over. Boats are hard.

28
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:21,380
Ollie: We need help. Let's ask Gran Mari.

29
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:33,890
Gran Mari: Well now, a muddy seagull and a gloomy crab. What's all this?

30
00:03:35,390 --> 00:03:39,550
Ollie: Gran Mari, why do boats float?

31
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:48,190
Gran Mari: Oh, that is a good question, Ollie. Let's find out together.

32
00:03:49,690 --> 00:03:59,460
Gran Mari: These are the same foil. I'll squeeze this one into a ball. I'll fold this one into a wide boat.

33
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:12,650
Gran Mari: First, the ball. Watch the water.

34
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:16,780
Ollie: The ball sinks!

35
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:23,850
Gran Mari: Now the boat. Same foil, same weight.

36
00:04:25,350 --> 00:04:27,650
Pip: The boat floats!

37
00:04:29,150 --> 00:04:44,200
Gran Mari: The wide boat pushes a lot of water aside. The water pushes back up and holds it. The small ball pushes only a little, so it sinks.

38
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:48,030
Gus: So my clay needed to be flat and wide?

39
00:04:48,430 --> 00:04:54,060
Gran Mari: Well now, what do you think happens next?

40
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:59,060
Ollie: If we flatten the clay, it will float!

41
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:18,080
Gran Mari: Too much on one side, and it tips. Not a mistake, just something to learn. So we try again.

42
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:35,260
Ollie: Try it at home! Fill a sink with water. Squeeze one piece of foil into a ball. Fold another into a wide boat.

43
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:46,080
Ollie: Set them on the water. The ball sinks. The boat floats! Add a few stones, one at a time.

44
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:58,020
Gus: Wait, before we go. I fibbed. My boat sank, and I said it was a submarine.

45
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:01,960
Gus: I'm sorry I said I meant to. I just wanted to be fast.

46
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:06,830
Ollie: Thanks for telling us the truth, Gus.

47
00:06:08,330 --> 00:06:11,480
Gus: It floats! My lump is a boat after all!

48
00:06:13,590 --> 00:06:15,390
Pip: What if it tips again?

49
00:06:17,590 --> 00:06:19,620
Bean: Try!

50
00:06:27,590 --> 00:06:30,980
Pip: I did it! I tried again, and it floated!

51
00:06:33,590 --> 00:06:39,750
Ollie: Can I ride along, Pip? You're the captain.

52
00:06:41,250 --> 00:06:45,220
Pip: Yes! Hop aboard, first mate.

53
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:52,110
Ollie: Time for my Wonder Pocket! Three things we learned.

54
00:06:58,610 --> 00:07:04,780
Ollie: One. A wide, light boat pushes the water aside and floats.

55
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:11,670
Ollie: Two. A small, heavy lump pushes less water and sinks.

56
00:07:13,170 --> 00:07:18,940
Ollie: Three. If a boat tips over, we can try again.

57
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:24,830
Ollie: And one kind thing to try today. Cheer on a friend who tries again.

58
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:32,460
Gus: Bye, everybody! Next time, I'll try the careful way too!
